00:47:06.690 --> 00:47:08.810
And they would rest their lives upon it.

00:47:10.090 --> 00:47:11.110
And so when we gather,

00:47:11.210 --> 00:47:12.470
when we do the things we do,

00:47:13.050 --> 00:47:14.450
when we lift up songs of worship,

00:47:14.450 --> 00:47:15.070
when we pray,

00:47:15.170 --> 00:47:16.490
when we gather on Sunday mornings,

00:47:16.630 --> 00:47:19.110
when we minister to one another in prayer,

00:47:19.190 --> 00:47:20.630
when we read the word together,

00:47:20.630 --> 00:47:25.510
when we do all of these things, can we have a sense it's not just about us here and now. We're

00:47:25.510 --> 00:47:32.010
part of something greater than ourselves. Let's join in that tradition of believers through the

00:47:32.010 --> 00:47:36.130
centuries, through the millennia, who have given their lives to Christ. In fact, they're staked

00:47:36.130 --> 00:47:41.610
their lives and their eternal hope upon him. That's what all of this is about. Stand firm.

00:47:41.690 --> 00:47:47.370
We need to have courage because while there is this certainty of eternal hope that we have,

00:47:47.370 --> 00:47:50.550
we also don't know when that rebellion will come.

00:47:50.630 --> 00:47:53.190
We don't know when that man of lawlessness will come.

00:47:53.310 --> 00:47:54.410
Will it be in our generation?

00:47:54.570 --> 00:47:55.150
Will it be in another?

00:47:55.270 --> 00:47:56.010
We don't know.

00:47:56.810 --> 00:47:58.570
But we always need to be ready for it.

00:47:58.950 --> 00:48:00.190
So stand firm.

00:48:01.030 --> 00:48:04.330
And Paul ends this chapter with a prayer for the Thessalonian church.

00:48:05.210 --> 00:48:06.470
Verse 16 and 17 again,

00:48:06.590 --> 00:48:09.370
Now may our Lord Jesus Christ himself and God our Father,

00:48:09.810 --> 00:48:13.290
who loved us and gave us eternal comfort and good hope through grace,

00:48:13.690 --> 00:48:17.730
Comfort your hearts and establish them in every good work and word.

00:48:19.110 --> 00:48:24.510
Paul is praying here in a way to remind the believers not to focus just on their situation,

00:48:25.830 --> 00:48:30.250
but to root their hope, to root their prayers in God and who his character is.

00:48:31.550 --> 00:48:34.470
This is about the Lord Jesus, God our Father.

00:48:34.610 --> 00:48:36.910
He gave us eternal comfort and hope and grace.

00:48:37.490 --> 00:48:39.230
He did all these things for us.

00:48:39.230 --> 00:48:45.230
and he says, he prays, comfort your hearts and establish them. So, you know, that word establish,

00:48:45.430 --> 00:48:52.630
it means strengthen. Strengthen them for the good work, the good word that the Lord has entrusted

00:48:52.630 --> 00:48:58.630
to you. And here as we close this out, even as we hear this prayer, as a prayer prayed for us,

00:48:59.050 --> 00:49:05.190
the church, can we think about and recognize there is a good work that the Lord has prepared for each

00:49:05.190 --> 00:49:10.750
of us to do. Probably not just one good work, probably many good works, many good words to

00:49:10.750 --> 00:49:16.550
share about Christ and what he has done. And so let's think about, is there a good work for the

00:49:16.550 --> 00:49:26.640
Lord that maybe you've grown weary of doing? I know many of us face that. There are times I face

00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:34.740
that. I'm like, God, I'm tired. I'm just tired. I don't know how to go on. Paul prays here for the

00:49:34.740 --> 00:49:42.480
church. We can take this as a prayer for ourselves. Be strengthened. Be established. Be strong in the

00:49:42.480 --> 00:49:50.000
Lord. Is there a good work the Lord has called you to that maybe you're avoiding? Maybe God showed

00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:55.800
you, spoke to you, challenged you, invited you. For whatever reason, you've been avoiding that

00:49:55.800 --> 00:50:02.060
call of Christ on your life. Is there a good work for the Lord that maybe you feel inadequate for?

00:50:02.060 --> 00:50:05.260
if you feel inadequate that's good

00:50:05.260 --> 00:50:06.740
you're in good company

00:50:06.740 --> 00:50:09.280
you're right there with everyone

00:50:09.280 --> 00:50:10.900
who said yes to the Lord before you

00:50:10.900 --> 00:50:13.120
feeling inadequate is not a reason

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:15.180
to not follow God's call

00:50:15.180 --> 00:50:17.080
or not do the work he's called you to

00:50:17.080 --> 00:50:18.500
all of us are inadequate

00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:22.540
have you been wandering away because of that

00:50:22.540 --> 00:50:24.860
here as we read this prayer

00:50:24.860 --> 00:50:26.360
stand firm

00:50:26.360 --> 00:50:28.780
pray, trust the Lord

00:50:28.780 --> 00:50:29.920
to empower you

00:50:29.920 --> 00:50:33.520
a lot of things we can say about the end times

00:50:33.520 --> 00:50:34.560
in the New Testament,

00:50:34.780 --> 00:50:36.440
but I'll maybe wrap up a little bit

00:50:36.440 --> 00:50:37.640
with this verse here

00:50:37.640 --> 00:50:39.860
that Jesus himself said in Mark 13, 33.

00:50:40.460 --> 00:50:41.060
Be on guard.

00:50:41.720 --> 00:50:42.280
Keep awake,

00:50:42.620 --> 00:50:43.700
for you do not know

00:50:43.700 --> 00:50:44.620
when the time will come.

00:50:45.640 --> 00:50:46.920
We don't need to make predictions.

00:50:47.740 --> 00:50:49.400
We don't need to try to figure it out

00:50:49.400 --> 00:50:50.740
by this verse and that verse

00:50:50.740 --> 00:50:52.120
and this number and that measurement

00:50:52.120 --> 00:50:53.220
and all this kind of stuff.

00:50:53.420 --> 00:50:54.100
We don't need to wait

00:50:54.100 --> 00:50:55.180
for a vision for the Lord.

00:50:56.560 --> 00:50:57.140
Be on guard.

00:50:58.060 --> 00:50:58.600
Keep awake.

00:50:59.420 --> 00:51:00.040
Stand firm.

00:51:01.460 --> 00:51:02.900
We don't know when the time will come.

00:51:03.520 --> 00:51:06.340
As one thing for today, don't be distracted or deceived.

00:51:06.760 --> 00:51:08.820
Stand firm as we wait for Christ's return.

00:51:09.380 --> 00:51:10.600
Don't be distracted or deceived.

00:51:10.820 --> 00:51:12.880
Stand firm as we wait for Christ's return.

00:51:14.440 --> 00:51:17.300
Pastor Sam mentioned last week that there are people in the world today

00:51:17.300 --> 00:51:18.900
who are living under persecution.

00:51:19.660 --> 00:51:24.000
And for myself, I think I find it encouraging, challenging, inspiring,

00:51:24.440 --> 00:51:27.680
and it moves me to pray when I hear the stories of people

00:51:27.680 --> 00:51:29.640
who are suffering for their faith in the world today.

00:51:29.840 --> 00:51:32.200
I'd like to close with just sharing one example of that with you.

00:51:32.200 --> 00:51:37.200
And this picture is of a woman named Helen Burhain, and she's from Eritrea.

00:51:37.440 --> 00:51:38.640
She's a gospel singer.

00:51:40.160 --> 00:51:46.400
And if you know about Eritrea, it's a country in Africa where there is quite a bit of persecution against Christians.

00:51:47.100 --> 00:51:48.620
I'll share a little bit of her story with you.

00:51:49.220 --> 00:51:53.420
Helen placed her faith in Jesus at eight years old while her parents were political prisoners.

00:51:54.000 --> 00:52:00.800
By the age of 14, she began writing her own worship music, and at 18, she began preaching the gospel in the streets of her city.

00:52:01.500 --> 00:52:03.620
In 2002, so this was happening a little while ago,

00:52:03.960 --> 00:52:06.720
some laws were passed in Eritrea against evangelism.

00:52:07.200 --> 00:52:11.820
And in 2004, the government closed Helen's church that she was part of,

00:52:11.900 --> 00:52:14.700
and they were not allowed to gather together anymore in person.

00:52:15.640 --> 00:52:19.600
Helen saw a need there, and so she decided to record a CD.

00:52:19.980 --> 00:52:21.240
People used CDs back then.

00:52:21.580 --> 00:52:23.760
She decided to record a CD of gospel music

00:52:23.760 --> 00:52:27.380
so that her church members could still worship the Lord at home,

00:52:27.780 --> 00:52:30.080
even while they weren't able to meet together in person.

00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:36.740
And this was found out, and so Helen was arrested shortly after the release of that CD as it was distributed.

00:52:37.480 --> 00:52:46.000
She was imprisoned for 32 months at the Mai Serwa prison in a steel shipping container that was her cell in the desert heat.

00:52:46.700 --> 00:52:51.100
She was chained to the wall and given minimal food, no bathroom to use.

00:52:51.980 --> 00:52:58.860
The guards beat her and told her that if she would just deny her faith and sign a document saying that she denied Christ,

00:52:58.860 --> 00:53:04.940
then she could be set free, but she refused to do so. Even while the guards were beating her with

00:53:04.940 --> 00:53:11.420
rods, Helen continued to sing songs of worship and to lift her eyes to the Lord. Eventually, the guards

00:53:11.420 --> 00:53:16.700
realized that she would not deny her faith in Christ and that she was near death, and so they

00:53:16.700 --> 00:53:24.800
released her and sent her home to die. But her family found her, and she fled to Sudan, and then

00:53:24.800 --> 00:53:29.420
she received asylum in Denmark, where she continues to worship and serve the Lord today.

00:53:30.800 --> 00:53:37.960
I share this story just partly as just awareness. I think it's important for us to be aware

00:53:37.960 --> 00:53:41.940
of what's going on in the world, aware of the sufferings of our brothers and sisters in Christ.

00:53:42.860 --> 00:53:46.960
But I think it's also a good encouragement to us to remember the things we read about in

00:53:46.960 --> 00:53:52.140
Scripture are not just 2,000 years away from us. People are living out their faith this way in

00:53:52.140 --> 00:53:58.360
the world today. And we don't know when that might come. We don't know where some of us here might be

00:53:58.360 --> 00:54:04.620
called. Some of us might be called to go to hard places, places where there is persecution, places

00:54:04.620 --> 00:54:09.640
where there are threats to our safety for following Christ. If that's the good work the

00:54:09.640 --> 00:54:15.800
Lord has called us to, whether it's here, whether it's far away, will we be those who stand firm?

00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:18.020
will we be those

00:54:18.020 --> 00:54:19.520
who say I'm not going to be

00:54:19.520 --> 00:54:20.960
distracted or deceived

00:54:20.960 --> 00:54:22.480
will we stand firm

00:54:22.480 --> 00:54:23.920
knowing our eternal hope

00:54:23.920 --> 00:54:25.540
is in Christ's return

00:54:25.540 --> 00:54:26.800
and so no matter

00:54:26.800 --> 00:54:27.500
what we go through

00:54:27.500 --> 00:54:28.140
in this life

00:54:28.140 --> 00:54:29.420
and say Lord

00:54:29.420 --> 00:54:30.500
I'm going to meet you

00:54:30.500 --> 00:54:30.980
one day

00:54:30.980 --> 00:54:32.240
I'm going to share

00:54:32.240 --> 00:54:32.960
in your glory

00:54:32.960 --> 00:54:34.760
it will all be worth it

00:54:34.760 --> 00:54:35.860
can we stand together

00:54:35.860 --> 00:54:36.540
as we respond

00:54:36.540 --> 00:54:37.460
to the Lord here today
